Sources for `security-audit` skill (see plans/skill-audits/security-audit.md for full audit):

- gstack /cso (v1.57.10, ~/.claude/skills/gstack/cso/) — the audit METHODOLOGY only: mode/scope resolution, the phase framework (0 stack model, 1 attack-surface census, 2-11 scope-gated audit, 12 FP filter + confidence gate + verification, 13 findings report). Its runtime plumbing (gbrain sync, telemetry, prior-learnings, plan-mode, voice, AskUserQuestion machinery, gstack-config/learnings binaries) is REJECTED, not vendored.
- OWASP Top 10 — https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/ — the A01-A10 categories in Phase 9.
- OWASP Top 10 for LLMs — https://owasp.org/www-project-top-10-for-large-language-model-applications/ — Phase 7.
- STRIDE (Microsoft threat-modeling) — Phase 10 component matrix.
- Snyk ToxicSkills research — the skill-supply-chain threat (Phase 8).

Strategy: distill (not compose-gstack). Unlike `security-guidance` which composed /cso for the deep pass, this skill IS the deep pass — the periodic ceiling, vendored in full so it survives the gstack teardown (epic DEV-383, Vague 1). gstack /cso becomes a dead reference; the four core skills that pointed at it now point here.

Deferred, not rejected: live-surface DAST (nuclei, live header/TLS probing, authenticated crawls). Belongs to the claude-in-chrome MCP re-point, epic DEV-383 Vague 4.
